# Learning Easy — Environment Variable Reference
#
# This is a CLIENT-SIDE ONLY application.
# There are no server-side environment variables.
#
# The only configurable secret is the Gemini API key, which is entered
# through the in-app ⚙ AI Settings modal and stored in the browser's
# localStorage (key: el20_geminiKey). It is NEVER committed to the repo.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO GET A FREE GEMINI API KEY
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# 2. Sign in with a Google account
# 3. Click "Create API key"
# 4. Copy the key
# 5. Open the app → click ⚙ in the header → paste the key → Save
#
# Free tier limits (as of 2026): 1 500 requests/day, 15 requests/minute
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIRD-PARTY APIS USED (no key required)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Translation:  https://api.mymemory.translated.net  (MyMemory — free, no key)
# Dictionary:   https://api.dictionaryapi.dev         (Free Dictionary API — free, no key)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXAMPLE (copy to .env if you add a build-time injection step later)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your key here
